{"id":"chatcmpl-379b2f3c-0741-4d24-8c2d-af181ab9217b","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244959,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When visual QA tools disagree on a binary finding, the task forces a side/option choice that requires resolving conflicts via independent verification against original pixels and orientation markers. The successful strategy combined multi-tool cross-validation with explicit laterality reasoning, ultimately trusting the tool that provided a specific anatomical localization over a null finding when forced-choice constraints applied.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Cross-validate critical findings with at least two independent visual QA tools before committing to an answer, especially when options force a choice between mutually exclusive findings.\",\n    \"When tools conflict, prioritize the output that provides specific anatomical localization (e.g., named vessel/region) over a null or vague finding, since forced-choice tasks imply a positive finding exists.\",\n    \"Always check for orientation/laterality markers (L/R labels) to correctly map image sides to patient anatomy before assigning left vs. right.\",\n    \"Use a verification step to inspect original pixels when tool outputs conflict, rather than defaulting to the first or most confident-sounding tool.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Query multiple vision-language models with the same structured question; require each to report presence, location, and laterality; reconcile disagreements by favoring specific localizations and confirming with orientation markers.\",\n    \"Forced-choice visual tasks\": \"Treat the option set as a prior that a positive finding exists; use it to break ties toward the tool that identifies a concrete finding rather than a null result.\",\n    \"Conflict resolution in tool orchestration\": \"When two tools disagree, escalate to a verification call that re-examines source data and explicitly states the conflict and risk before finalizing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm at least two independent tools agree on presence and laterality, or document why one was favored.\",\n    \"Verify orientation markers (L/R) are identified and used to map image side to patient anatomy before answering.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":617,"total_tokens":1017,"completion_tokens":400,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":617},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":400}}}